cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, data or these results, please cite them as below."
title: "The Hadwiger–Nelson problem: an exact, certificate-driven attack"
abstract: >-
  Exact-arithmetic tools, data and machine-checked certificates for the
  Hadwiger–Nelson problem on the chromatic number of the plane. Includes proofs
  that the planes over Q(sqrt3, sqrt11) and Q(sqrt2, sqrt3) are 4-chromatic,
  reproductions of chi(R^2) >= 4 and >= 5 with DRAT certificates, and
  two-distance witnesses for the route to chi(R^2) >= 6. AI-assisted research;
  not peer reviewed.
type: software
authors:
  - alias: decalion89
repository-code: "https://github.com/decalion89/darwin-50"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-09-25"
keywords:
  - Hadwiger–Nelson problem
  - chromatic number of the plane
  - unit-distance graphs
  - graph colouring
  - SAT solving
  - DRAT proofs
  - algebraic number theory
  - p-adic fields
